1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,440
Finding a way back up was rough, so of course when we try to go back down, we run into something like this.

2
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:10,800
I don't like it at all.

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:12,820
This blood hasn't dried yet.

4
00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:16,560
Fallon must have passed through recently to head to the lower floors.

5
00:00:17,880 --> 00:00:19,580
I bet she was cramped in here.

6
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:26,420
The sixth floor. Underground waterways that utilize tunnels dug by ancient dwarves.

7
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:32,300
They appear to stretch out endlessly, laying themselves under the town like the roots of a tree.

8
00:00:33,060 --> 00:00:36,400
Besides the water, many things likely flowed through here.

9
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:38,420
Humans and animals.

10
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:41,140
Conspiracies and rumors.

11
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:44,000
Money and blood.

12
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:46,360
It's so cold.

13
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:49,360
Yeah, it's weird since I'm pretty sure this floor is supposed to be humid.

14
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:52,520
Maybe we ended up somewhere else?

15
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:54,880
I think. I remember this road from before.

16
00:00:55,480 --> 00:01:00,200
Yeah, this is definitely the floor where the red dragon attacked us and almost wiped out our party.

17
00:01:00,960 --> 00:01:03,500
I mean, it is a dungeon where walls and roads move around.

18
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:05,820
The temperature changing isn't that strange.

19
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:08,820
I prefer it being cold over it being hot.

20
00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:12,340
But the snow and water washing away the bloodstains is a big problem.

21
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:16,340
Since we're here, do we want to head back to the place where we almost got wiped?

22
00:01:16,340 --> 00:01:20,540
If the dungeon cleaners haven't gotten to it yet, we might be able to salvage our stuff.

23
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:22,720
I wonder if Fallon is doing okay.

24
00:01:22,720 --> 00:01:25,780
I'd imagine this cold is pretty tough on red dragons.

25
00:01:26,040 --> 00:01:27,600
Wait, is that why she had feathers?

26
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:33,040
So, Laios, since you got in Shuro's face and blurted out we were going to defeat the mad mage,

27
00:01:33,380 --> 00:01:35,340
surely you must have some kind of plan, right?

28
00:01:36,020 --> 00:01:37,340
Yeah, about that.

29
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,780
Fallon said she was looking for someone named Delgol.

30
00:01:40,780 --> 00:01:44,860
I imagine the mad mage had given the red dragon that same order.

31
00:01:45,660 --> 00:01:50,300
That's also the reason the red dragon came up to a different floor and wandered around without resting.

32
00:01:51,660 --> 00:01:52,700
Who's Delgol?

33
00:01:52,940 --> 00:01:55,860
The name sounds familiar, but I'm drawing a blank.

34
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:56,900
It's the king.

35
00:01:56,900 --> 00:02:02,760
When the golden country fell 1,000 years ago, he was their last ruler.

36
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:07,660
You can find engravings in various spots of this dungeon that sing his praises.

37
00:02:07,820 --> 00:02:08,580
Oh, that's right.

38
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:10,860
His name is on artifacts that have been dug up.

39
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:12,000
Hang on.

40
00:02:12,280 --> 00:02:13,960
But didn't I hear that he...

41
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:20,440
Yeah, when this dungeon was initially discovered, he briefly appeared on the surface, became dust, and vanished.

42
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:26,240
So, the mad mage has been working the red dragon to the bone and completely changing the dungeon's structure,

43
00:02:26,660 --> 00:02:29,000
all to find a king who disappeared ages ago?

44
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:32,960
Ever since the mad mage witnessed the previous king get killed right in front of him,

45
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:35,500
he's worried that his son will meet the same fate.

46
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:39,940
That's why he must have assumed we were assassins and started attacking us.

47
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:42,640
Really? Where'd you hear that from?

48
00:02:43,040 --> 00:02:43,580
A dream?

49
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:49,440
Oh, uh, well, you see, I first met the mad mage inside of the living paintings,

50
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:50,980
and that's where I learned about it.

51
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:52,020
Remember?

52
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:55,700
I told you that I tried to eat some food in there, and he was so pissed at me.

53
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:57,000
What?

54
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:58,640
Why didn't you mention that so much?

55
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:00,700
I only put the pieces together just now.

56
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:02,720
Huh, I see.

57
00:03:03,140 --> 00:03:04,720
So you were reliving the past.

58
00:03:05,340 --> 00:03:09,120
To be absolutely sure, you said that the mad mage was an elf, right?

59
00:03:09,420 --> 00:03:11,460
Do elves really live up to 1,000 years?

60
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:13,600
There were records of it a long time ago.

61
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:17,180
But currently, our typical lifespan is about 500 at best.

62
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:18,620
At best, huh?

63
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:21,800
Well, I mean, you're able to mess with other people's lives,

64
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:24,920
so I'd imagine it's simple enough for you to extend your own.

65
00:03:25,180 --> 00:03:26,100
That's not true.

66
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:28,860
It's impossible to prolong your life with your own magic.

67
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:31,980
That'd be like someone trying to eat their own flesh to live longer.

68
00:03:31,980 --> 00:03:36,000
Anyway, if he attacked us because he thought that we were enemies of the king,

69
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:38,080
maybe we can clear things up with him.

70
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:38,680
Mm-hmm.

71
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:46,260
The wind's gotten way stronger!

72
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:47,860
Why is it so cold?

73
00:03:47,980 --> 00:03:49,100
I can't see ahead.

74
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:50,440
Hey, you guys!

75
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:52,040
Are you still following me?

76
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:53,520
Ariel, where did you go?

77
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:54,900
I can't see anything.

78
00:03:55,260 --> 00:03:56,960
It'd be bad if we got separated.

79
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:58,820
Grab onto someone's hand!

80
00:03:58,820 --> 00:04:11,140
We can't go on like this.

81
00:04:12,820 --> 00:04:13,740
A tunnel!

82
00:04:14,460 --> 00:04:15,400
Let's take shelter!

83
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:25,580
You guys okay?

84
00:04:26,280 --> 00:04:26,640
Chill?

85
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:27,720
I'm here.

86
00:04:28,180 --> 00:04:28,880
No issues.

87
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:30,100
Marcelle?

88
00:04:30,580 --> 00:04:31,060
Present.

89
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:32,460
I'm over here!

90
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:33,640
Senshi?

91
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:34,580
Yeah.

92
00:04:34,940 --> 00:04:35,560
All good.

93
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:37,320
Oh, thank goodness.

94
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:38,820
Hey, Marcelle.

95
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:39,380
Wait a sec.

96
00:04:39,380 --> 00:04:40,620
Could you give us some light, please?

97
00:04:40,620 --> 00:04:40,700
Yes!

98
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:51,000
This place, it kind of looks like an old prison.

99
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:54,320
For a while there, I thought we...

100
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:58,380
No way!

101
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,320
This is...

102
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:03,500
We've multiplied!

103
00:05:04,880 --> 00:05:06,640
Hey, the hell is all this?

104
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:07,840
Illusion magic?

105
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:09,560
Let's see.

106
00:05:11,980 --> 00:05:15,080
My guess is, it's the work of a shapeshifter.

107
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:16,360
Shape what?

108
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:17,460
Never heard of them.

109
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:20,120
Where I'm from, they're monsters that appear sometimes.

110
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:24,400
On days when the fog is thick or there's a heavy snowstorm,

111
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:27,120
walk through the hills and you'll suddenly have extra companions.

112
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:30,100
That's when the shapeshifter copies your appearance

113
00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:31,960
and blends themselves with the rest of your group.

114
00:05:32,060 --> 00:05:34,040
Wherever you're from, sounds scary.

115
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:35,920
Is it some type of fairy?

116
00:05:36,180 --> 00:05:37,740
Are they prone to causing trouble?

117
00:05:37,980 --> 00:05:40,440
If they go unnoticed, they'll kill and eat the real one

118
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:41,280
and take their place.

119
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:42,200
What the hell?

120
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:44,300
We have to hurry and find the fake ones!

121
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:44,540
Huh?

122
00:05:46,080 --> 00:05:47,580
I must eat.

123
00:05:47,900 --> 00:05:49,200
Well, this isn't good.

124
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:51,800
Hey, those Lioses over there?

125
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:54,380
I think it's pretty safe to say they're fake.

126
00:05:54,760 --> 00:05:55,620
Sounds about right.

127
00:05:56,220 --> 00:05:58,420
Yeah, they don't look like they know much about monsters.

128
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:01,700
Shapeshifters will read the minds of living creatures,

129
00:06:01,980 --> 00:06:03,900
mimicking the appearance of those around them.

130
00:06:03,900 --> 00:06:06,560
So the three other me's over there

131
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:09,680
reflect how the real Senshi, Marcille, and Chilchuk remember me.

132
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:11,920
That makes sense.

133
00:06:12,260 --> 00:06:13,340
If you look closely,

134
00:06:13,460 --> 00:06:16,200
you can see each version looks somewhat different than the rest.

135
00:06:17,160 --> 00:06:19,500
Can we hurry and do something about this one, then?

136
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:20,120
Huh?

137
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:22,060
She's clearly a fake.

138
00:06:22,680 --> 00:06:23,440
Sure is.

139
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:26,840
How dare you gaze upon my visage and see that I am the...

140
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:28,200
Ugh, so annoying.

141
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:30,140
Whose memory did she come from?

142
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:32,780
This Senshi and Chilchuk are clearly fakes as well.

143
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:34,380
How so?

144
00:06:34,700 --> 00:06:35,000
Huh?

145
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:36,140
Just look at him!

146
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:38,740
My neck wrap isn't a scarf, but his is.

147
00:06:38,740 --> 00:06:40,760
And Senshi's helmet's missing holes.

148
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:44,800
Now that you mention it...

149
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:47,840
I don't think there's any doubt that they're from Laios' memory.

150
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:49,780
He's not great with details.

151
00:06:52,740 --> 00:06:54,720
Is it fine to leave them like that?

152
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:57,620
They don't really have the same intelligence a human does.

153
00:06:58,280 --> 00:07:01,140
But if you do try to attack them, they're sure to fight back.

154
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:04,820
Let's avoid fighting unknown monsters under these circumstances.

155
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:08,840
We'll reveal the fakes peacefully and then deal with them all!

156
00:07:10,760 --> 00:07:13,520
His enthusiasm's great, but...

157
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:16,840
Will he really be able to tell the difference between the real one and the fakes?

158
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:17,760
Not likely.

159
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:21,580
The number of fakes remaining is six.

160
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:25,020
When they're side by side, you can see lots of differences.

161
00:07:25,700 --> 00:07:28,960
But while we're figuring this out, our fuzzy memories are being influenced.

162
00:07:29,560 --> 00:07:31,540
I need to hurry and settle this or else.

163
00:07:32,140 --> 00:07:34,980
When it comes to the Marcells, they have different hairstyles.

164
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:38,380
I honestly don't remember what her hair looked like when I last saw her.

165
00:07:38,380 --> 00:07:39,160
You're kidding!

166
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:42,280
This hairstyle's unique, so you remember it, don't you?

167
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:43,160
Just look at it!

168
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:45,560
The blizzard made me cold, so I took my hair down.

169
00:07:45,860 --> 00:07:48,080
First of all, my hair quality is way better.

170
00:07:48,340 --> 00:07:50,180
Hair is a magic user's life, you know.

171
00:07:50,640 --> 00:07:52,920
They're all saying things the real one would say.

172
00:07:53,300 --> 00:07:56,500
Well, they are acting the way we see Marcell in our heads.

173
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:00,620
Oh, here's an idea!

174
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:04,120
How about we decide based on information that only I would know?

175
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:07,180
I hope you don't mean stuff like guessing your mom's maiden name.

176
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:07,920
Not that.

177
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:10,960
Look at my spell book!

178
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:13,780
You see?

179
00:08:14,940 --> 00:08:17,180
Yeah, one of those books is obviously fake.

180
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:19,640
Hard to tell with the other two.

181
00:08:19,740 --> 00:08:20,680
They both look legitimate.

182
00:08:20,960 --> 00:08:21,260
What?

183
00:08:21,460 --> 00:08:22,160
No way!

184
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:24,180
The spells in her book are all messed up!

185
00:08:24,240 --> 00:08:25,480
Hey, that's my line!

186
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:29,760
Our personal belongings might help reveal more fakes.

187
00:08:30,140 --> 00:08:31,660
Senshi, mind showing your stuff?

188
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:38,260
Lock them up with the others!

189
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,480
We've narrowed it down to two each, but...

190
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:47,640
We're at a standstill.

191
00:08:48,300 --> 00:08:49,660
Number of fakes remaining?

192
00:08:50,660 --> 00:08:51,180
Three.

193
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:51,340
Three.

194
00:08:51,340 --> 00:08:54,920
Okay.

195
00:08:55,360 --> 00:08:56,320
Let's make food.

196
00:08:56,740 --> 00:08:58,360
Wait, at a time like this?

197
00:08:58,760 --> 00:09:00,800
I can't tell you apart based on looks.

198
00:09:01,260 --> 00:09:03,480
So now I've got to check for usual behavior.

199
00:09:04,420 --> 00:09:07,540
I'll have all of you cook and observe how you do things.

200
00:09:08,100 --> 00:09:10,140
That will tell me which are fake and which are real.

201
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:17,000
He didn't know he encountered the Mad Mage or noticed Shuro's feelings.

202
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:20,580
He didn't pick up on the fact that he'd already met that Cobber guy either.

203
00:09:20,580 --> 00:09:23,920
And we're going to rely on his observational skills.

204
00:09:27,080 --> 00:09:28,100
This is bad.

205
00:09:29,540 --> 00:09:32,200
Who are my party members and who are the impostors?

206
00:09:32,760 --> 00:09:35,060
It's my chance to regain the trust that I lost.

207
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:37,160
I really don't want to disappoint them again.

208
00:09:37,860 --> 00:09:40,660
I have to pick up on the subtle differences no matter what.

209
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:43,060
We're dealing with Laius.

210
00:09:43,420 --> 00:09:46,980
There's a possibility he might find the fakes more interesting because they're monsters.

211
00:09:48,020 --> 00:09:48,840
That's true.

212
00:09:48,840 --> 00:09:51,540
Well, we have to do something about this ourselves.

213
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:54,220
I'll be watching from here.

214
00:09:54,700 --> 00:09:55,960
So do your best, everyone.

215
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:57,060
Gee, thanks.

216
00:09:57,400 --> 00:09:58,440
What should we make?

217
00:09:58,840 --> 00:10:00,680
There's what I found on the fifth floor.

218
00:10:01,260 --> 00:10:04,280
And the ingredients Maizuru was kind enough to give to us.

219
00:10:05,100 --> 00:10:09,100
With such good provisions on our hands, I've got an idea of what to make.

220
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:14,620
Before you all start, pair up with your other self and work as a team to prepare a dish.

221
00:10:14,620 --> 00:10:19,940
By having you perform the same assignment, I can watch for different behaviors.

222
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:22,080
Senshi can teach you the recipe.

223
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:25,800
Now that's settled, is everyone ready?

224
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:27,820
Let the cooking begin!

225
00:10:27,820 --> 00:10:31,600
First, the Chilchuk team.

226
00:10:32,660 --> 00:10:35,840
Cut the meat, and then mix the eggs and seasonings.

227
00:10:36,640 --> 00:10:38,180
Chilchuk A sat in the hallway.

228
00:10:38,900 --> 00:10:41,700
Chilchuk B sat on top of a wooden box and started prepping.

229
00:10:42,560 --> 00:10:43,840
What are you even writing?

230
00:10:43,900 --> 00:10:44,700
You're distracting.

231
00:10:44,700 --> 00:10:50,660
I won't budge.

232
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:51,800
Can you get it, Laios?

233
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:52,560
Huh?

234
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:54,200
Hey, you see that?

235
00:10:54,380 --> 00:10:55,180
B slipped up!

236
00:10:55,220 --> 00:10:56,140
He's the fake one!

237
00:10:56,400 --> 00:10:56,740
Huh?

238
00:10:56,880 --> 00:10:58,100
What are you talking about?

239
00:10:58,320 --> 00:10:59,240
Oh, come on!

240
00:10:59,300 --> 00:11:00,220
You guys know me!

241
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:02,800
I've got lots of conviction and pride and all that!

242
00:11:02,980 --> 00:11:05,440
It's important that people help each other, Chilchuk.

243
00:11:05,900 --> 00:11:07,920
A's a little cynical, don't you think?

244
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:10,840
If you look closely, he's got some mean-looking eyes.

245
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:11,620
Hey!

246
00:11:12,460 --> 00:11:14,520
Our Chilchuk is definitely much cuter!

247
00:11:14,700 --> 00:11:15,460
Leave me alone!

248
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:18,580
Hey, Laios, you know I'm the real one, right?

249
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:20,780
Chilchuk A.

250
00:11:21,260 --> 00:11:24,060
He does have a pretty suspicious-looking face.

251
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:25,720
He might be the fake.

252
00:11:26,420 --> 00:11:27,080
We'll see.

253
00:11:27,460 --> 00:11:28,660
Please continue cooking.

254
00:11:30,260 --> 00:11:30,820
Dumbass.

255
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,880
Insulted me in the common language.

256
00:11:34,960 --> 00:11:36,460
Next, the Marsil team.

257
00:11:37,060 --> 00:11:39,560
I'm sorry, but what is this egg that we're using?

258
00:11:39,860 --> 00:11:40,960
It's a harpy egg.

259
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:46,760
I've said this plenty of times since the start, that humanoid monsters are off-limits!

260
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:49,320
Yes, I've started to compromise, but it's still not okay!

261
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:53,820
Marsil B. is behaving normally, but maybe to a fault.

262
00:11:54,260 --> 00:11:55,080
Back to the recipe.

263
00:11:55,620 --> 00:11:56,940
Boil the dice dryads.

264
00:11:56,940 --> 00:11:59,700
What do you think, Marsil A?

265
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:06,880
I don't like it, but I've already eaten fishmen eggs and dryads, so why bother complaining now?

266
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:10,200
If it meant that I could save Fallon, then I'd do anything.

267
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:15,960
Hey, I would also do anything to save Fallon, you know?

268
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:18,320
P's determination is weak in comparison.

269
00:12:18,420 --> 00:12:21,240
Do I have to eat these harpy eggs to make you believe me?

270
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:27,500
When the eggs are soft enough to pierce with a chopstick, drain the water, mix with the seasonings, and mash.

271
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:30,080
Wait, this is actually tough.

272
00:12:30,680 --> 00:12:32,580
They both said things the real one would say.

273
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:34,260
Back to the sentry team.

274
00:12:34,260 --> 00:12:37,540
So, where did you get those harpy eggs from, anyway?

275
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:43,280
I came across a nest inside of a collapsed house, so I gathered everything that was there.

276
00:12:44,020 --> 00:12:45,640
Cut to one centimeter thick.

277
00:12:46,580 --> 00:12:49,640
As they say, eggs are the perfect...

278
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:51,040
Source of nutrients.

279
00:12:52,660 --> 00:12:55,340
Fry with rice on low heat, and then season.

280
00:12:56,340 --> 00:12:58,680
I'm pretty sure rice is Shuro's favorite food.

281
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:03,100
It's packed with plenty of essential nutrients adventurers need to explore.

282
00:13:03,100 --> 00:13:05,780
We were real lucky to find as much as we did.

283
00:13:06,580 --> 00:13:10,180
I'm only interested in eating monsters we find, but Senshi's different.

284
00:13:10,600 --> 00:13:14,860
He's focused on deeper things, like taking flavor and nutrition into account.

285
00:13:15,820 --> 00:13:17,500
All the food looks so good.

286
00:13:17,940 --> 00:13:19,740
Guess I can't decide based on skill.

287
00:13:21,260 --> 00:13:25,360
You know, no one's really said anything about it, so I thought I'd check.

288
00:13:25,900 --> 00:13:29,780
But doesn't Senshi B look a little more attractive than he should?

289
00:13:30,780 --> 00:13:31,340
Whoa!

290
00:13:33,100 --> 00:13:35,860
Seems fine to me.

291
00:13:36,420 --> 00:13:38,040
Yeah, Senshi's always looked handsome.

292
00:13:39,160 --> 00:13:41,900
What even is this, prejudice against dwarves?

293
00:13:41,980 --> 00:13:44,180
Yeah, come on, Senshi doesn't look that dopey.

294
00:13:44,820 --> 00:13:46,360
Senshi is handsome.

295
00:13:46,960 --> 00:13:47,240
Noted.

296
00:13:47,780 --> 00:13:48,100
Mm-hmm.

297
00:13:48,100 --> 00:13:52,780
Vyos, the food's almost ready.

298
00:13:53,180 --> 00:13:54,780
Have you made your final decision yet?

299
00:13:55,780 --> 00:13:56,220
Honestly?

300
00:13:57,020 --> 00:13:58,240
I have no idea.

301
00:13:58,820 --> 00:14:00,360
They all look like they could be real.

302
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:01,200
Or fake.

303
00:14:02,060 --> 00:14:07,360
Besides, I think it's kind of unfair to have me try to distinguish a memory in my head against the actual thing.

304
00:14:07,360 --> 00:14:14,360
It would have been fun to look for a monster disguised as a human, but trying to see through an illusion is...

305
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:17,420
Look for a monster, huh?

306
00:14:18,100 --> 00:14:18,960
It's ready!

307
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:23,960
All right.

308
00:14:24,460 --> 00:14:25,660
Listen up while you eat.

309
00:14:26,460 --> 00:14:27,960
Those of you I think are real are...

310
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:33,080
Kill Chuck A, the one with the dour expression.

311
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:38,060
Marsil B, the one who won't eat harpy eggs even if it's for Fallon.

312
00:14:38,980 --> 00:14:41,180
Senshi A, the dopey one.

313
00:14:41,860 --> 00:14:45,380
That said, will the impostors promptly lock themselves in the cell?

314
00:14:45,380 --> 00:14:46,640
Now hold on a second!

315
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:49,400
What kind of proof do you have that he's a real one?

316
00:14:49,700 --> 00:14:51,860
That one's obviously the impostor!

317
00:14:52,300 --> 00:14:53,720
What makes you think she's real?

318
00:14:54,280 --> 00:14:56,040
Mm, just a feeling.

319
00:14:56,700 --> 00:14:58,580
I'll try to explain all of that later.

320
00:14:59,340 --> 00:15:00,780
Let's deal with the fake ones first.

321
00:15:02,280 --> 00:15:03,920
It's... just a feeling?

322
00:15:04,760 --> 00:15:05,460
Deal with?

323
00:15:06,040 --> 00:15:07,740
I knew it, this guy's a joke.

324
00:15:08,540 --> 00:15:12,080
It seems like we're just gonna have to protect ourselves.

325
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:12,580
Ah!

326
00:15:15,380 --> 00:15:18,320
This was inevitable, no matter who I picked.

327
00:15:19,500 --> 00:15:22,180
Shapeshifter is a term for monsters that mimic others.

328
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:27,300
There are kinds that can mimic voices or possess or physically change their appearance.

329
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:30,000
Which is this Shapeshifter capable of?

330
00:15:30,940 --> 00:15:33,560
There's no way that monsters are able to cook food.

331
00:15:34,320 --> 00:15:36,540
It must be creating an illusion like Marsil said.

332
00:15:37,540 --> 00:15:41,260
Since it targets people, it's either a carnivore or an omnivore.

333
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:44,700
It's too much of a coward and lacks the strength to attack directly.

334
00:15:45,380 --> 00:15:48,100
Visibility's low, and it's cold here.

335
00:15:48,620 --> 00:15:52,020
So it can withstand the cold and relies on smell and hearing.

336
00:15:53,660 --> 00:15:54,000
Hmm.

337
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:56,620
Downwind is that direction.

338
00:15:57,280 --> 00:16:00,140
The enemy's waiting for us to wear ourselves out.

339
00:16:00,140 --> 00:16:03,620
I doubt I'll hit it by recklessly swinging my sword around.

340
00:16:04,660 --> 00:16:05,660
So what should I do?

341
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:08,180
Kensuke's gotten pretty quiet.

342
00:16:08,980 --> 00:16:10,200
He might die from the cold.

343
00:16:11,780 --> 00:16:13,880
Guess I'll have to take a page from the enemy.

344
00:16:14,400 --> 00:16:17,720
Time to turn the tables and make the hunter feel like the hunted.

345
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:21,280
It's been a while, but I'll do that.

346
00:16:21,280 --> 00:16:44,160
A dog?

347
00:16:44,740 --> 00:16:45,100
What?

348
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:47,040
Wait, a hunting dog?

349
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:51,140
For as long as I can remember, dogs have always been by my side.

350
00:16:51,380 --> 00:16:52,740
And I've learned a lot from them.

351
00:16:53,420 --> 00:16:54,080
How to hunt.

352
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:56,760
How to engage with a threat stronger than you are.

353
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:59,560
And now, let me teach you!

354
00:17:01,140 --> 00:17:02,060
He's good.

355
00:17:02,260 --> 00:17:03,520
Bayos really is.

356
00:17:03,660 --> 00:17:04,280
A dog.

357
00:17:04,760 --> 00:17:08,520
You may think you're the hunter, but you're actually the one being hunted!

358
00:17:08,520 --> 00:17:09,520
Everyone!

359
00:17:11,520 --> 00:17:12,580
Look!

360
00:17:12,760 --> 00:17:13,400
The illusions!

361
00:17:26,300 --> 00:17:28,640
So you've finally shown yourself.

362
00:17:29,080 --> 00:17:33,320
Since you're a beast, you should know full well in this fight.

363
00:17:33,320 --> 00:17:38,460
The one who flinch is first is the one who loses!

364
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:41,480
Bayos now!

365
00:17:41,480 --> 00:17:41,980
No!

366
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:07,500
You all right, Laios?

367
00:18:08,020 --> 00:18:09,420
All right in the head, that is?

368
00:18:10,200 --> 00:18:10,640
Uh-huh.

369
00:18:11,480 --> 00:18:13,180
There's a lot of things I want to say,

370
00:18:13,460 --> 00:18:15,120
but how come you didn't draw your weapon?

371
00:18:15,540 --> 00:18:17,480
Honestly, I got too into character.

372
00:18:18,180 --> 00:18:18,520
Ah!

373
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:18,980
Huh?

374
00:18:21,400 --> 00:18:23,600
Look what happened to all the food we made.

375
00:18:23,880 --> 00:18:25,860
Makes sense since we cooked it with an illusion.

376
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:27,440
Let's remake it.

377
00:18:29,360 --> 00:18:32,020
Man, hard to believe that Laios' intuition

378
00:18:32,020 --> 00:18:33,300
was actually on the nose.

379
00:18:33,660 --> 00:18:35,380
So how did you tell us apart?

380
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:38,180
By the lack of monster awareness?

381
00:18:39,140 --> 00:18:39,420
Huh?

382
00:18:39,420 --> 00:18:43,140
Well, first, Chilchuk sat on a wooden box.

383
00:18:43,800 --> 00:18:46,500
Boxes are the perfect hiding spot for mimics and tentacles.

384
00:18:47,260 --> 00:18:49,860
For you to not even worry about that kind of stuck out to me.

385
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:53,360
I came across a nest inside of a collapsed house.

386
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:55,740
So I gathered everything that was there.

387
00:18:55,740 --> 00:18:58,940
For someone who respects the balance of an ecosystem,

388
00:18:59,220 --> 00:19:00,460
that seemed a bit careless.

389
00:19:01,100 --> 00:19:03,980
Do I have to eat these harpy eggs to make you believe me?

390
00:19:04,780 --> 00:19:07,200
Lastly, when Marsil dumped the boiling water.

391
00:19:07,820 --> 00:19:09,600
After how you were attacked by that undine,

392
00:19:09,860 --> 00:19:11,580
doing something like that seemed reckless.

393
00:19:12,260 --> 00:19:13,560
That's why it caught my attention.

394
00:19:13,560 --> 00:19:22,060
In this case, it was that absent-mindedness

395
00:19:22,060 --> 00:19:23,800
that made me think you were the real one.

396
00:19:24,160 --> 00:19:24,640
Huh.

397
00:19:25,480 --> 00:19:26,940
That was some good work.

398
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:28,900
I'm real proud of you, Laios.

399
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:31,940
I think his perspective is still a bit off.

400
00:19:31,940 --> 00:19:36,320
Well, still, it's not easy to see through an illusion spell.

401
00:19:37,060 --> 00:19:39,420
It did keep the shapeshifter fed, after all.

402
00:19:40,300 --> 00:19:41,780
I thought you noticed, then.

403
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:44,720
I've already eaten fishmen eggs and dry eggs.

404
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:47,660
When she mentioned the fishmen eggs in particular,

405
00:19:48,500 --> 00:19:49,700
it should have been obvious.

406
00:19:50,100 --> 00:19:52,460
I mean, we've never eaten those kinds of eggs before.

407
00:19:52,660 --> 00:19:53,280
Right, guys?

408
00:19:53,280 --> 00:20:00,220
Could it have been that barley dish?

409
00:20:02,660 --> 00:20:04,520
The dessert's ready now, too.

410
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:05,220
All right!

411
00:20:06,040 --> 00:20:08,300
It's been a while since we've had sweets.

412
00:20:08,620 --> 00:20:09,560
Should I make some tea?

413
00:20:10,220 --> 00:20:11,720
Pretty sure there were tea leaves

414
00:20:11,720 --> 00:20:13,280
in the bag of provisions we got.

415
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:14,200
Hmm?

416
00:20:15,060 --> 00:20:16,680
Did you put it somewhere else?

417
00:20:17,220 --> 00:20:19,660
No, I definitely put it right here.

418
00:20:19,980 --> 00:20:20,340
Hmm?

419
00:20:23,280 --> 00:20:25,120
The rice.

420
00:20:40,840 --> 00:20:41,960
Empty.

421
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:48,520
Marcel!

422
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:48,720
Marcel!

423
00:20:49,920 --> 00:20:51,880
Drop your weapon and freeze.

424
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:54,460
Do that, and we can talk peacefully.

